    "title": "Who is Alex Cooper? How to watch 'Call Her Daddy' podcast hosted by former MA resident",
    "text": "Feb. 12, 2025, 12:25 p.m. ET\"Call Her Daddy\" is an interview-style podcast hosted by Alex Cooper.Cooper graduated from Boston University in 2017, where she played soccer.The show routinely hosts high-profile guests, including former Vice President Kamala Harris.Between interviewing a presidential candidate and inking a business deal reportedly worth $125 million, Alex Cooper has come a long way from her days as a college student in Boston.Dubbed \"Gen Z's Barbara Walters\" by Rolling Stone, Cooper hosts the mega-viral podcast \"Call Her Daddy.\" The show started in 2018 as an advice podcast hosted by Cooper and her former friend Sofia Franklyn.In the years since, \"Call Her Daddy\" and Cooper have garnered cult-like followings, making the show one of the most popular podcasts on Spotify.What's the hype about? Here's what to know about Cooper and \"Call Her Daddy.\"Who is Alex Cooper? Her Boston tiesCooper is from Newtown, Pennsylvania, but relocated to Massachusetts to attend Boston University. At BU, she played soccer and graduated with a bachelor's degree in film and television in 2017.She said in a 2023 interview with Vanity Fair that her athletic career taught her skills that she still uses in her business.“Aside from the classic grit, tenacity, and determination, I am so competitive now with myself,\" Cooper said. \"I had to advocate for myself with authoritative figures since I was 12. Now I’m able to mold myself depending on who I’m speaking to.”However, Cooper has also opened up about traumatic experiences she had while playing soccer at BU. She told Cosmopolitan in 2023 that she was \"in the process\" of healing from that time.\"Recently, I reconnected with a lot of the people that I played soccer with who were around when things were happening and it’s been pretty cathartic,\" she said. \"I met up with one of my teammates in Santa Monica who I hadn’t seen since we graduated—we didn’t even say hi, we just both started crying.\"In addition to hosting \"Call Her Daddy,\" Cooper has a podcast network called The Unwell Network and a media company with her husband, Matt Kaplan, called Trending. She also has a beverage line called Unwell Hydration.What is 'Call Her Daddy'?\"Call Her Daddy\" is an interview-style podcasted hosted by Cooper. The show launched in 2018 as a sex positivity and advice podcast from Cooper and her former cohost, Franklyn.However, in recent years, Cooper has shifted the tone of the show to feature high-profile guests opening up about their personal lives, like Miley Cyrus, Hailey Bieber and most recently, Kylie Kelce. She also released an interview with then-presidential candidate Kamala Harris in October 2024.The show was formerly owned by Barstool Sports before Cooper left the company for a $60 million exclusive deal with Spotify in 2021. Last year, after her contract with the streaming service expired, she signed a distribution deal with SiriusXM reportedly worth $125 million.\"Call Her Daddy\" has consistently been ranked as one of the most popular podcasts on Spotify and releases new episodes every Wednesday on YouTube, Spotify and Apple.Melina Khan is a trending reporter for the USA TODAY Network - New England, which serves more than a dozen affiliated news organizations across New England. She can be reached at MKhan@gannett.com.",
